cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use isa-lm in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "isa-lm: a portable C11 runtime for INT8/INT4 Llama-style language model inference on legacy x86-64 and ARM instruction sets"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Park
    given-names: Yeochoon
    alias: JonPark0
repository-code: "https://github.com/JonPark0/isa-lm"
url: "https://jonpark0.github.io/isa-lm/"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-27"
abstract: >-
  isa-lm is a dependency-free C11 inference runtime for Llama-style decoder Transformers
  with INT8 (Q8_0) and INT4 (Q4_0) weights, mixed Q4/Q8 models and an optional Q8 KV cache.
  The code targets a portable baseline and binds every operator at compile time to the
  best kernel for the chosen instruction set, with no runtime dispatch: x86-64 from SSE2
  through SSE4.1, AVX2, AVX-VNNI and AVX-512 VNNI, and ARM from ARMv7 NEON through ARMv8.2
  dot product, i8mm and SVE. Weights are repacked into row-interleaved layouts for the
  integer dot-product instructions of each ISA, prompts are prefilled in batches, the
  weight stream is prefetched in software, and attention is blocked for grouped-query heads.
  Results are bit-identical across thread counts and batch sizes and are checked against a
  numpy reference forward pass. It reads llama2.c checkpoints, Hugging Face safetensors
  (including Llama 3 RoPE scaling) and Hugging Face tokenizer.json files (SentencePiece-style
  and Llama 3 byte-level BPE, identical to the tokenizers library), and includes a chat mode,
  a perplexity tool and a CPU feature guard that refuses unsupported processors.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM inference
  - CPU inference
  - quantization
  - INT8
  - INT4
  - mixed precision
  - SIMD
  - SSE2
  - AVX2
  - AVX-512 VNNI
  - ARM NEON
  - SVE
  - i8mm
  - legacy hardware
  - edge computing
  - Llama
  - C11
